# Docusaurus RTL CSS (Persian / fa)

This site is RTL-only (`i18n.defaultLocale: fa`, `direction: rtl`). Docusaurus runs **RTLCSS** on CSS and flips physical values.

## What gets flipped (broken if written naively)

| You write | Built CSS becomes |
| --- | --- |
| `text-align: right` | `text-align: left` |
| `direction: rtl` | `direction: ltr` |
| `padding-left` / `margin-right` | swapped |

This made doc **title** and **description** appear LTR until fixed.

## Correct patterns

Prefer **logical properties** (not flipped incorrectly):

```css
text-align: start; /* right in RTL */
margin-inline-start: 0;
padding-inline-end: 0;
border-inline-start: 1px solid ...;
```

When you must force physical RTL, wrap with ignore:

```css
/*rtl:begin:ignore*/
html[dir='rtl'] .docItemTitle,
html[dir='rtl'] .docItemDescription {
  text-align: right;
  direction: rtl;
}
/*rtl:end:ignore*/
```

## Do not

- Set `direction: rtl` on doc content without `rtl:ignore` — it becomes `ltr` and breaks Persian layout.
- “Fix” LTR by adding more `text-align: right` without checking the **built** CSS in `build/assets/css/`.

## Working header pattern

Doc pages use swizzled `src/theme/DocItem/Content/index.tsx` to render frontmatter `title` + `description` as `.docItemTitle` / `.docItemDescription`, styled with the `rtl:ignore` block in `src/css/custom.css`.
